# .gitignore — agnostic pop-gen pipeline (scripts-only, data excluded by default)
# Generated via the repo-scaffold skill's default, plus this pipeline's specifics.
# Aggressive by design. To publish ONE small synthetic/public file, un-ignore it
# explicitly, e.g. when the tiny test cohort lands:  !tests/tiny_cohort/toy.vcf.gz

# === Research data & large/binary outputs — never commit ===
data/
raw/
results/
output/
outputs/
*.csv
*.tsv
*.xlsx
*.parquet
*.feather
*.rds
*.RData
*.rda

# Genomics formats
*.fastq
*.fq
*.fastq.gz
*.fq.gz
*.bam
*.sam
*.cram
*.bai
*.crai
*.csi
*.vcf
*.vcf.gz
*.bcf
*.bed
*.bim
*.fam
*.ped
*.gff
*.gtf
*.fasta
*.fa
*.fna
*.fai
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.npy
*.npz

# === Secrets / credentials ===
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
*.p12
credentials
.netrc
.pgpass
service-account*.json
.aws/
.ssh/

# === Sample sheets / metadata (un-ignore deliberately if truly safe) ===
*sample_sheet*
*samplesheet*
*manifest*
*barcodes*

# === Pipeline run artefacts ===
logs/
reports/
.snakemake/

# === Solved environment — the manifest + lock are tracked, the env is not ===
.pixi/

# === Python ===
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# === R ===
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.Ruserdata

# === OS / editor / logs ===
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
*.log

# === Internal dev briefs — kept local, never published ===
briefs/

# === Transient artefact from the data-layout migration (remove on host) ===
data_old_symlink

# === Tiny synthetic test cohort — safe to commit (it's fake) ===
# Un-ignore the fixture inputs so the smoke test is self-contained. Run
# artefacts (outputs/logs/reports beneath tests/tiny_cohort) stay ignored
# via the top-level outputs/, logs/, reports/ patterns above.
!tests/tiny_cohort/data/
!tests/tiny_cohort/data/**
!tests/tiny_cohort/config.yaml
!tests/tiny_cohort/generate.py
!tests/tiny_cohort/README.md

# === Environment manifest (agnostic/env/) — tracked on purpose ===
# The `venv/` patterns above must not swallow this directory. Named file by
# file rather than with `!env/**`, so default-deny still applies to anything
# that lands in here later (a stray .env, a key, a data file).
!env/
!env/README.md
!env/postinstall.sh
!env/check_env.sh
!env/environment.yml

# === Public pull-and-play example (examples/) — the sanctioned exception ===
# This is the ONE place a VCF + metadata are committed, and it is safe because
# every sample is a published ENA accession and every field is public. The
# default-deny patterns above (data/, *.vcf.gz, *.csi, *.tsv, *.list) would
# otherwise swallow all of it, so each committed file is un-ignored BY NAME —
# never with a glob, so a stray file dropped into examples/data/ is still
# ignored by default. examples/build_example.sh re-derives these and asserts
# zero overlap with the embargoed cohort before it writes them.
!examples/data/
!examples/data/vcf/
!examples/data/vcf/example.vcf.gz
!examples/data/vcf/example.vcf.gz.csi
!examples/data/metadata/
!examples/data/metadata/samples.tsv
!examples/data/reference/
!examples/data/reference/regions_to_mask.list
!examples/ACCESSIONS.tsv
# The reference FASTA is NOT shipped — it is ~24 MB and users fetch it from
# PlasmoDB (examples/README.md). Keep it ignored even though it sits here.
examples/data/reference/*.fasta
examples/data/reference/*.fasta.fai

# Snakemake writes this into any directory() output (e.g. docs/steps/)
.snakemake_timestamp
